- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/curl.html
- Summary (EN): Computes the curl of an input vector field, which measures its circulation and therefore local rotation. Available since Houdini 22.0.
- Résumé (FR) : Calcule le rotationnel d'un champ vectoriel pour repérer les rotations locales.

- Inputs meaning: ["v: a UV layer or a Vector VDB containing the vector field (only input)"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Space: Image, Pixel or Local coordinate space for the computation", "Scale: constant multiplier applied to the curl", "Kernel Size: maximum neighbour distance, in buffer elements, used for derivatives", "Read Pixels outside Image: reads beyond the image edge for Wrap borders, off for Clamp borders"]

- Caveats: ["A UV input gives a mono 2D scalar curl; a Vector VDB input gives a Vector VDB 3D curl.", "Results depend on Space and border settings, so magnitudes are not directly comparable across configurations."]

